      "passive_list": {
        "0": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p>Once before the next rest, after making an Initiative Check as leader or a Check to&nbsp;<br>examine someone or something, the target may add a bonus of +4 to the Result of&nbsp;<br>the Check.</p>",
          "passive_name": "Planning",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        },
        "1": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p>Once before the next rest, if you are about to suffer one or more status effects from&nbsp;<br>the same source, you may instead choose not to suffer any of those status effects.</p>",
          "passive_name": "Training",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "camp activity"
        },
        "2": {
          "$deleted": false,
          "passive_description": "<p>When you acquire this Quirk, choose Dexterity, Insight, Might, or Willpower.<br>When you join a conflict scene, you may choose one option: you increase the chosen<br>Attribute by one die size until the end of the scene (up to a maximum of d12); or, if the<br>chosen Attribute's base die size is d12, you increase it by one die size until the end of<br>the scene (up to a maximum of d20).</p>\n<p>When you choose one of the above options, the Game Master gains an opportunity<br>which can be spent during the current scene or later, to showcase the unexpected<br>collateral effects of your abilities (such as drawing the attention of a psychic entity,<br>alerting the authorities to your presence, or damaging the continuum).</p>",
          "passive_name": "NEO-HUMAN",
          "passive_roll": "",
          "passive_source": "quirk"
        }
      },
